# Wilvor documentation

Before the first documentation edit in a session, read and follow `docs/DOCUMENTATION_STANDARDS.md`. That file is the canonical standard: headings, links, Mermaid, maturity labels, the page template, the source-reference convention, and file ownership.

## Scope

Apply this rule only to Markdown documentation you are writing or editing.

Do not use this rule to refuse, narrow, or block Python, TypeScript, Terraform, tests, scripts, or infrastructure work. When the task is software implementation, implement it.

When the task is documentation, do not modify Python, TypeScript, Terraform, tests, operational scripts, or infrastructure. Do not run Terraform apply, deployment scripts, AWS-mutating commands, or external live validation.

## Claims and maturity

Read the implementation symbol before stating behavior. Read the test assertion before applying UNIT, CONTRACT, INFRA, or INT. Search the Terraform roots before applying TF.

Use only these labels, and only after that check: CODE, TF, UNIT, CONTRACT, INFRA, INT, LIVE, DEPLOYED, PLANNED, UNKNOWN.

Keep these as separate facts: code existence, test coverage, Terraform configuration, deployment, and production authorization. TF does not establish DEPLOYED. A live harness does not establish a current pass or a production grant. UNKNOWN stays UNKNOWN.

Cite claims with the source-reference convention in the standards file. Repository-relative paths and symbols. Do not invent files, routes, counts, or resources.

## Aviation, review, and evidence

Preserve advisory decision support and qualified human review. Deterministic services remain authoritative. Do not document a clearance, ATC instruction, flight-control instruction, landing instruction, altitude instruction, reroute, or infrastructure mutation as a Wilvor capability.

Re-read `MasterRouteExecutionAuthority` before writing an execution value. At the standards baseline it is `DENIED` only, and production execution is not representable.

Do not upgrade confidence, freshness, tool status, or provenance. Supplied evidence metadata is not an authenticated read. Missing versions, timestamps, and limitations stay missing. Model output is not an operational fact.

## Existing pages and ownership

On a behavior page, include Implementation status and Known limitations. Use the page template for new pages.

Do not delete historical README or review text. Move a superseded current claim under Historical record and cite the replacement.

Edit only files on your workstream list in the standards. Do not edit `docs/DOCUMENTATION_STANDARDS.md` or this rule during parallel documentation work. Do not edit another workstream's files. Link to `functions/shared/wilvor_operational/README.md`; do not rewrite it.
